@startuml ChoiceuiFlock
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: a cbirds-derived ambient flock in the choice prompt, ported as a technique rather than adopted as code
' covers: internal/choiceui/flock.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/layout.go, internal/choiceui/choiceui.go
' covers: internal/run/choices.go
' covers: internal/choiceui/flock_test.go, internal/choiceui/layout_test.go

' ── WHY A PORT, NOT THE PROGRAM ────────────────────────────────────────────
' cbirds (github.com/clainstone/cbirds, MIT) is one C99 program with no
' library API: it owns the terminal itself through its own VT layer.
' Vendoring it needs cgo, and internal release builds set CGO_ENABLED=0
' for linux, darwin, freebsd and windows on two architectures, while
' cbirds builds only on linux and macOS. Bundling it as a side binary
' breaks the flat single-binary CDN artifact the installer ships.
' What transfers is the technique, which is Reynolds 1987 plus a braille
' cell packing. Both re-implement in pure Go inside the tcell screen
' proveo already owns, under the palette and tiers proveo already has.

' ── WHERE IT MAY LIVE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The prompt hands the terminal to the agent harness when it closes, and
' ptyproxy owns that screen afterwards. An overlay then is impossible
' without intercepting agent output, which pty-ownership forbids. The
' only ambient surface is the choice form itself, while the operator
' decides. The flock is therefore a region of that form, opt-in per form
' through Form.Flock, and the run form is its first and only customer.

' ── THE LADDER DECIDES, THE FLOCK NEVER PUSHES ────────────────────────────
' A tagline, flockRows and a separating blank cost six rows,
' charged in the banner's place in the drop ladder in layout.go: an
' afforded flock replaces the banner box instead of stacking under it,
' because charging both put the flock past the height of a typical
' terminal and it was silently never seen. The header is the product
' tagline alone — the box and the wordmark both go. It still ranks below every
' informative region — axis, header and strip all outrank it — and it
' holds no reserved slot: help keeps its maximum, the body keeps its
' floor, and the hint stays pinned above both.

' ── TWO CLOCKS, THREE TIERS ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' cbirds repeats the simulation sixty times a second (FRAME_RATE in
' boids.c). The strip stays on animFrame, 120ms, so a mote still walks
' one cell per strip frame. A form with Form.Flock posts at flockFrame
' (time.Second/60) instead. flockTick is that count. The strip's frame()
' is still time.Since/animFrame, so the faster poster does not speed
' the motes. The event queue is ten deep and shared with keystrokes, so
' the poster keeps a single interrupt queued: frame() drops the latch
' when the loop reads the clock, and a tick that arrives while one is
' unread is dropped. The clock is read at draw time, so a dropped post
' loses no sky. flockSim advances by the delta since its last flock
' frame, capped at five strip frames (flockMaxDelta) so a stalled
' terminal does not fast-forward on wake. Each step integrates the
' gains that were tuned at 120ms, scaled by flockStep, so a bird covers
' the same dots per second and the braille picture changes on most of
' the sixty paints. GlyphsNerd and GlyphsSafe pack cells
' as braille: two by four dots per cell, rune U+2800 plus the dot
' bits, which the glyph ban in tui-design-language leaves legal.
' Braille carries no emoji
' presentation and its width is one column in every font that has it.
' GlyphsASCII degrades a cell to '.' for a sparse cell and '*' for a
' dense one. GlyphsOff affords no region at all, matching how the tier
' strips every other mark rather than redrawing it plainer.

' ── THE SIMULATION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Deterministic from a fixed seed, so a test paints the same sky as a
' run at the same tick. Each bird steers by separation, alignment and
' cohesion over neighbours inside a perception radius, with a boundary
' pull inside the margin, an acceleration cap (the turn limit that
' keeps fronts curved rather than snapping) and a speed band. The bird
' count scales with width and is capped, keeping the neighbour scan
' cheap at 60Hz. Positions live in dot space, not cells, so
' motion is smooth at sub-cell resolution and only the packing quantises.

title An ambient flock for the choice prompt, ported from cbirds

component "cbirds\nC99 · MIT · own VT layer\nno library API" as CBIRDS <<cloud>>
component "internal/choiceui flockSim\nboids in dot space\ndeterministic seed" as SIM <<app>>
component "braille packing\n2x4 dots per cell\nU+2800 + dot bits" as PACK <<app>>
component "layout drop ladder\nflock takes the banner's place\nsix rows, tagline kept" as LADDER <<app>>
component "Form.Flock opt-in\nrun form only" as FORM <<app>>
component "flock clock\n60Hz post, one interrupt queued\nstrip frame stays 120ms" as TICK <<async>>
database "tcell screen\nthe screen proveo owns\nuntil the prompt closes" as TERM <<db>>

CBIRDS ARROW_OPTIONAL SIM : technique only — boids + packing
SIM ARROW_MAIN PACK : dot grid
PACK ARROW_MAIN TERM : one rune per cell
LADDER ARROW_MAIN PACK : affords or omits whole
FORM ARROW_MAIN LADDER : asks, never insists
TICK ARROW_QUEUE SIM : advances by flock-tick delta

note right of CBIRDS
  **Not adopted as code.** cgo would break
  the ""CGO_ENABLED=0"" release matrix, and a
  bundled side binary would break the flat
  CDN artifact. MIT would permit either;
  the release model forbids both.
end note

note right of SIM
  **Same tick, same sky.** A fixed seed and
  a capped tick delta make every frame a
  function of the frames before it, so tests
  assert motion without a clock or a screen.
end note

note bottom of PACK
  **Braille is legal here.** U+2800 carries
  no emoji presentation and measures one
  column. ASCII tiers get '.' and '*';
  the Off tier gets no region at all.
end note

note bottom of LADDER
  **The banner's place, not its own.**
  Six rows buy the flock only after body,
  hint, help and strip are afforded, and
  the banner box then stays home — but the
  tagline rides above the birds.
end note

note bottom of FORM
  **One customer, on purpose.** The run
  form opts in. Init and wizard forms do
  not: a flock under a credential field
  would decorate a secret, not a wait.
end note

@enduml
